From 3333333333333333333333333333333333333333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: waveshare: attach the DSI peripheral from probe

The driver registers and attaches its MIPI-DSI peripheral from
.bridge_attach, which only works for DSI hosts that expose themselves as a
plain drm_bridge (samsung-dsim, the platform it was written for).

On msm the DSI host joins the DRM device through the component framework and
only calls component_add() from its mipi_dsi_host .attach callback, so
attaching from .bridge_attach deadlocks: the component master waits for the
DSI component, which waits for the master to bind and attach this bridge.
The display never comes up and the DPU keeps deferring. Every other DSI
bridge used on msm (ti-sn65dsi86, lontium-lt9611uxc, ...) attaches its DSI
peripheral from probe for this reason.

Move the attach to the end of probe, after the drm_bridge is registered, so
the host can bind the bridge as soon as the peripheral attaches.

While here, check the first I2C write: the bridge board is part of the panel
assembly, so a NAK means no panel is plugged into the DSI connector. Bailing
out with -ENODEV leaves the DSI host unattached instead of streaming video
into a disconnected connector, which keeps a board that boots without a panel
behaving exactly as it did before the panel was described in DT.

Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/waveshare-dsi.c
@@ -80,11 +80,6 @@
 				   enum drm_bridge_attach_flags flags)
 {
 	struct ws_bridge *ws = bridge_to_ws_bridge(bridge);
-	int ret;
-
-	ret = ws_bridge_attach_dsi(ws);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;

 	return drm_bridge_attach(encoder, ws->next_bridge,
 				 &ws->bridge, flags);
@@ -171,7 +166,10 @@
 		return ret;
 	}

-	regmap_write(ws->reg_map, 0xc0, 0x01);
+	ret = regmap_write(ws->reg_map, 0xc0, 0x01);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "no bridge board on the connector\n");
+
 	regmap_write(ws->reg_map, 0xc2, 0x01);
 	regmap_write(ws->reg_map, 0xac, 0x01);

@@ -179,7 +177,14 @@
 	ws->bridge.of_node = dev->of_node;
 	devm_drm_bridge_add(dev, &ws->bridge);

-	return 0;
+	/*
+	 * Attach the DSI peripheral here and not from bridge_attach: a DSI host that
+	 * joins its DRM device through the component framework (msm) only registers
+	 * its component once a peripheral attaches, so attaching from bridge_attach
+	 * cannot work - the component master would be waiting for the DSI component
+	 * that is waiting for the master to attach this bridge.
+	 */
+	return ws_bridge_attach_dsi(ws);
 }

 static const struct of_device_id ws_bridge_of_ids[] = {
